From 26776e168ae7d4d038e6f0fe122fe9421ac993f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <mia.ailab1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 16:37:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 18/25] glm cuda: E4M3 sequences on KV pages: page layout,
 placement, snapshots, TF_KV_PAGES=on, over-pool refusal

- A page's part a DSA layer holds is its E4M3 codes (512 x 512 B), their fp32 scales (512 x 4 B), then
  the pooled index keys: 296,960 B, 580 B a token (pageCacheBytes). pageBytesOf adds the target MTP
  head's part only when it is loaded, so beside DFlash2 a token takes 6,380 B (bf16 keeps its layout).
- State records its format and head (kv8, head); onPages places lc, ls and pk; initPagedFormat and
  pagedBytesOf; cuda_pages makes every paged sequence in the engine's format.
- Kept states copy paged scales by their own span (snapshot layout), so the cache and the host tier
  keep and restore E4M3 prefixes through the pages as through a window.
- TF_KV_PAGES=on (1, all) pages E4M3 too; auto keeps E4M3 on windows; unknown values are refused by name
  (BadKvPages) instead of read as on.
- A request needing more pages than the whole pool holds is admitted and refused (PoolTooSmall, with
  words) instead of waiting in the queue forever.

The kernels' launchers (cuda_latent, cuda_sparse) come separately; until then an E4M3 pass on pages is
refused there (Fp8OnPages).

